Structure of the tool_calls response:
```json
{
  "message": {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "",
    "tool_calls": [
      {
        "function": {
          "name": "...",
          "arguments": {...}   // object (in the native API, not a string)
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "done_reason": "stop"/"tool_calls",
  ...
}
```

Note: in the newer documentation, tool calls include `"type": "function"` and `index` inside function. In issue #6462 (older version), there was no type/index. The current docs show a format that includes type and index. Also note that arguments is an object rather than a JSON string like OpenAI's. Furthermore, the tool result message uses role: "tool" with tool_name (not tool_call_id).

